"""Advanced single-file semiconductor process simulation platform with UI.

This implementation follows the architectural blueprint described in
"半导体工艺模拟软件设计蓝图.md". It delivers a voxel-based, modular TCAD-like
experience inside one Python script, combining a physics-inspired simulation
kernel with a PyQt5 user interface. Supported process modules cover
lithography (spin, exposure, develop), etch (dry/wet/plasma), deposition (PVD,
CVD, ALD, epitaxy), chemical-mechanical planarization, ion implantation, and
post-implant annealing/oxidation. A recipe editor, parameter inspector,
and multi-view visualization (3D stack, cross-section, doping heatmap) help
users configure and analyse virtual film stacks while respecting the blueprint's
MVC mindset.

Key techniques implemented:
- Voxel grid wafer model with material palette, open mask tracking, doping and
  temperature fields.
- Optical aerial-image approximation using FFT-based Gaussian blur derived from
  illumination parameters, paired with a Dill-like resist development heuristic.
- Directional vs. conformal deposition heuristics and anisotropic etch removal
  governed by per-material rate data.
- CMP Preston law approximation with material selectivity look-up.
- Ion implantation depth distribution using Gaussian straggle and anneal-driven
  diffusion smoothing.

The UI ensures almost every operation is configurable through input widgets,
including domain sizing, recipe editing, parameter tuning, and measurement.
"""
